1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lauri_Pihkala '''Lauri "Tahko" Pihkala'''] (born Gummerus) was the inventor of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pes%C3%A4pallo pesäpallo], the Finnish variant of baseball. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pihkala participated''' in the Olympic Games in 1908 and 1912, competing in Jump, Discus, Shot put, and 800 m run. . 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In the 1910s''' he became the first Finnish professional coach in athletics, and also worked as a physical education instructor with the Finnish Army. Pihkala was known for being an avid sports fan, and he developed several out
2 CONC door games, not just pesäpallo.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pihkala was''' also a right-wing political activist. He supported eugenics as a means to improve the military prowess of the Finnish people.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During the''' [https://www.geni.com/projects/Suomen-sis%25C3%25A4llissota-1918/45794 Finnish Civil War] in 1918 he was responsible for propaganda in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Guard_(Finland White Guard] flying un
2 CONC it "''Devils of Kuhmoinen''" of major [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Kalm Hans Kalm]. In March 1918 Pihkala participated in a massacre in Harmoinen village in Finland. Patients and nurses in a field hospital for red fighters 
2 CONC were murdered.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1969 he''' became one of the first persons to receive an honorary doctorate in Sport Sciences from the University of Jyväskylä, together with president [https://www.geni.com/people/Urho-Kaleva-Kekkonen-8th-President-of-Finla
2 CONC nd/6000000011285570299 Urho Kekkonen] and Professor Kaarina Kari.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Memorial of''' Pihkala by sculptor Nina Sailo was unveiled in 1988 on the south-east side of the Helsinki Olympic Stadium.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fi.billiongraves.international/grave/Lauri-Pihkala/27236453
